id: pm-gantt-chart-uncertainty-intervals
title: Render reproducible completion intervals for declared scheduling uncertainty
description: Accept bounded estimate ranges or declared distributions and retain assumptions and seed in a scenario receipt.
type: Feature
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-22T16:07:49.861Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-23T15:25:04.784Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-23T15:25:03.362Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-23T15:25:03.362Z"
author: codex-agent
acceptance_criteria: Synthetic schedules reproduce quantiles; missing estimates remain unknown; sensitivity results identify which estimate dominates the interval.
comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-22T16:07:54.711Z",codex-agent,"Overlap check: existing gantt bars, schedule and repair use point estimates. Core graph SDK supplies deterministic registry-aware ordering and estimate/deadline analysis, without distribution sampling or completion quantiles. pm-graph renders graph analytics. pm-rl evaluates/trains learned policies; this feature samples caller-declared scheduling uncertainty and trains no model. Reuse certified complete-list reads, PmClient contracts/custom predecessors, RelationshipGraph and analyzeRelationshipExecution; keep the development SDK pin unchanged. Design: independent bounded uniform/triangular estimates, deterministic seeded sampling, explicit unknown propagation, compact quantiles and Pearson sensitivity, replayable scenario receipt. Local targeted checks; full npm and Bun release gates in CI."
  "2026-10-22T16:18:36.616Z",codex-agent,"Implemented typed completionIntervals SDK and gantt uncertainty command. Targeted uncertainty suite: 29 pass; simulation source measured 100% lines/branches/functions. Existing repair and smoke regressions: 36 pass. Three behavioral reverts are caught: midpoint sampling, missing effort becoming zero, and discarded sensitivity association (node test/revert-uncertainty.ts). Public tracker validation at d999e65: 18 active items, 14 unknown estimates/completions, baseline project finish unknown. Explicit hypothetical ranges, seed 42 and 10000 draws: P10/P50/P90 10.894413/50.703685/89.778522 days; dominant pm-gantt-chart-2u8i, Pearson 0.9999986156; compact JSON 9616 bytes. Repeated receipt is identical; durable tracker documents are unchanged; no git executable is available during reads. Full gates pending CI."
  "2026-10-22T16:21:54.297Z",codex-agent,"Linked tracker test execution passed all 65 targeted tests; automatic result persistence is disabled by existing project policy, so this comment retains the counts. Final simulation-only measurement after numerical hardening remains 29/29 and 100% lines/branches/functions. Typecheck, test typecheck, lint, docstrings and zero-duplication checks pass. Local strict health reports inherited global extension host-version skew and generated merge-fence drift; neither history repair nor merge-driver work is in scope. Fresh CI provisions its own dependencies and is authoritative for full npm/Bun and strict health evidence. No SDK/CLI defect was found in the feature path. npm ci required ignoring the local user npm configuration after EALLOWSCRIPTS in git dependency preparation; dependency pins are unchanged."
  "2026-10-22T16:27:27.844Z",codex-agent,"CI release evidence for implementation c43ca3e: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/actions/runs/39813599550 passed. Node 22.18.0 coverage: 315 tests passed; Node 26 npm run release:check and bun run release:check: 315 tests passed each, zero failures/skips, 100% lines/branches/functions across all four shipped sources. Strict CI tracker health, fresh dist verification, packed npm/Bun/minimum-host acceptance and all unchanged release gates passed. Added one further analytic parallel-join/diamond regression; it passes locally and proves max-branch completion plus one shared prerequisite draw. The final head reruns CI including this extra case. PR: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/pull/166. Automated review providers were unavailable or budget-limited; their statuses are not review approval. Feature acceptance is satisfied; keep item in progress for orchestrator verification."
  "2026-10-22T19:02:20.410Z",codex-agent,"Review round for PR 166: inspected all unresolved threads and every comment (two threads, no additional pages) plus the latest CodeRabbit review body; no outside-diff findings were reported. Both findings are valid: the estimate-file early refusal omits host remediation, and localeCompare changes seeded draw assignment and sensitivity ties across host locales. Plan: share locale-independent code-unit ordering, preserve remediation on file refusals, add real-locale and no-git refusal regressions with function-only behavioral revert proofs, rebuild dist and verify unchanged npm/Bun release gates. Remote branch is current and has no commits behind main."
  "2026-10-22T19:04:31.835Z",codex-agent,"Review round: both unresolved findings verified against the current head (PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vU7YJ and PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vU7YS). File refusals now supply the same remedy and host remediation; all refusal paths are checked in the real no-git tracker harness. Seed assignment, prerequisites and sensitivity ties now use a shared UTF-16 code-unit comparator. A regression executes real en-US, sv-SE and tr-TR ICU default locales with mixed-case/non-ASCII ids and compares full results/receipts and zero-correlation tie order. Added isolated behavioral reverts for each changed sorting site and the file-remediation field. No additional same-class defects found in the feature diff; test-only durable snapshots compare files within one process and do not assign scenario draws."
  "2026-10-22T19:07:42.082Z",codex-agent,"Review revert proof: node test/revert-uncertainty.ts passed all six probes. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vU7YS: reverting only active-task sorting to localeCompare fails the real-locale regression; restoring it and reverting only sensitivity tie sorting independently fails the same regression. PRRT_kwDOSYpIas6vU7YJ: removing only remediation from the estimate-file refusal fails the real no-git tracker regression. Each failure is an assertion, with no test/SDK mocks; both source files are restored in finally. Original quantile, unknown and sensitivity reverts still fail as expected. Source/test typechecks, lint, docstrings and 0% duplication pass; committed dist rebuilt. No outside-diff findings were reported, and no other same-class defect was found in the feature diff. Full npm/Bun release gates will run in CI per the original shared-host constraint."
  "2026-10-22T19:08:49.776Z",codex-agent,"Review validation complete locally: tracker-linked node --test test/uncertainty.test.ts test/deadline-repair.test.ts test/smoke.test.ts passed 67 tests, zero failures/skips (85 seconds under shared-host load; no timeout). node test/revert-uncertainty.ts caught all 6/6 behavioral reverts, including independent sort-site and remediation probes for both review threads. npm ci, build, source/test typechecks, lint, docstrings and unchanged zero-duplication check passed; no dependency/threshold change. Final npm/Bun gate run URLs and measured counts are retained in the PR 166 body for the exact pushed head: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/pull/166. Keep this item in progress for owner verification; review threads are intentionally not replied to or resolved."
  "2026-10-22T19:19:31.424Z",codex-agent,"Issue 167 follow-up: read the full issue and its comments, then ran its exact public-SDK source reproduction on current head 7742e831aefa1c062595bd6b69d0a129b828ec79 before editing. The code-unit comparator already resolves it: both Unicode row orders return identical complete results and hash 7a629a1a72c6f05c29c03f6c3b6d753a0edaaed0ec8109432e69a98e15073e9f; composed-id P50 is 5.636664288816974 days in both calls. Added an exact composed/decomposed Unicode-id regression with an ordinary ASCII control, checking both distinct ids are retained, per-id quantiles, receipt hash, sensitivity and full-result invariance. Added an isolated revert probe restoring localeCompare only at active-task sorting. No further runtime change is needed. Evidence: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-gantt-chart/issues/167. One issue comment will be posted after the final-head npm/Bun CI gate passes; the issue and review threads remain open."
  "2026-10-22T19:22:55.125Z",codex-agent,"Issue 167 regression and revert proof passed: test name is issue 167: composed and decomposed Unicode ids preserve per-ID quantiles when rows reverse. It uses exactly U+00E9 and U+0065/U+0301, seed 42, 1000 samples and [480,4800] minute ranges, plus an ordinary ASCII control. Restoring only localeCompare at active-task sorting makes the new test fail on per-id completion equality; restoring the existing code-unit comparator passes. node test/revert-uncertainty.ts caught all 7/7 probes and restored the runtime files. The exact regression passed via the pm test runner (one selected test, zero failures/skips); build, source/test typechecks, lint, docstrings and 0% duplication pass. Runtime and dist contents are unchanged. Final-head npm/Bun gate URLs/counts will be retained in PR 166 and the single requested issue 167 comment. No publication is claimed; no issue or review thread will be closed/resolved."
  "2026-10-23T15:24:47.102Z",codex-agent,"DELIVERED: merged PR #166 (e50a1af0da498e76c6443babd254f13bfed7d416) is an ancestor of audited main 9c887a56a99c7108591d9f223d09e3937ecf3e55. Inspected on main: test/uncertainty.test.ts, docs/uncertainty-intervals.md. Analytic seeded quantile/replay, missing/downstream unknown estimates and dominating sensitivity regressions are present, including exact Unicode-id order invariance. This tracker audit inspected existing tests/files; it does not claim a new full product test run."
